            <ArticleTitle>Ultrasonography and pediatric caudals.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>97-9, table of contents</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1213/01.ane.0000287681.41646.b8</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ultrasound is an important tool for performing pediatric regional blocks, including caudal blocks. We present a case in which the availability of ultrasound allowed us to proceed with a successful caudal block which we otherwise might have abandoned in an infant with difficult anatomy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
